1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:03,084
Pak Non's full name is Samad Bin Man.

2
00:00:03,693 --> 00:00:06,206
But people usually call me Pak Non.

3
00:00:06,773 --> 00:00:08,488
Pak Non originally comes from Perlis,

4
00:00:08,568 --> 00:00:10,946
Kampung Tok Kaya, Kayang, Perlis.

5
00:00:11,793 --> 00:00:16,366
Pak Non started making these wau (kites) with Pak Non's grandfather.

6
00:00:17,111 --> 00:00:18,216
Pak Non makes wau,

7
00:00:18,296 --> 00:00:20,884
because initially, it was my grandfather who flew wau.

8
00:00:21,331 --> 00:00:23,555
You could say he flew them every year,

9
00:00:23,635 --> 00:00:27,106
back when Pak Non was still little, around 8 or 9 years old.

10
00:00:27,391 --> 00:00:28,783
I was still in school.

11
00:00:28,863 --> 00:00:30,413
But it wasn't Pak Non who made the wau,

12
00:00:30,493 --> 00:00:32,091
at that time Pak Non just helped him.

13
00:00:32,171 --> 00:00:34,146
I would help launch the wau for my grandfather.

14
00:00:34,226 --> 00:00:36,719
My grandfather couldn't launch it alone,

15
00:00:36,799 --> 00:00:38,199
these wau require two people to launch.

16
00:00:38,776 --> 00:00:42,171
Starting from there, Pak Non became interested in making wau.

17
00:00:43,956 --> 00:00:45,023
It has been 60 years.

18
00:00:45,536 --> 00:00:47,786
Pak Non has been making wau for 60 years up until now.

19
00:00:48,910 --> 00:00:50,260
So, at that age,

20
00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:52,439
when Pak Non was in his teens,

21
00:00:52,519 --> 00:00:54,169
that's when I started making them with Tok Wan (grandfather).

22
00:00:55,130 --> 00:00:58,047
A person from Kota Bharu often brought him carved kites (wau sobek).

23
00:00:58,652 --> 00:01:01,084
Pak Non went straight to his house. To go learn.

24
00:01:01,570 --> 00:01:03,274
But the learning didn't take long;

25
00:01:03,354 --> 00:01:05,404
I stayed for a week, then returned to Perlis.

26
00:01:05,494 --> 00:01:07,094
So if there were people from Kelantan

27
00:01:07,174 --> 00:01:09,424
coming to sell cloth or heading back to Kelantan,

28
00:01:09,504 --> 00:01:10,769
Pak Non would follow them.

29
00:01:11,321 --> 00:01:12,469
So you could say

30
00:01:12,549 --> 00:01:14,099
it was from Kelantan that the knowledge

31
00:01:14,179 --> 00:01:15,761
of making these floral patterns

32
00:01:15,841 --> 00:01:17,241
was learned by Pak Non.

33
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:21,126
These wau, based on their patterns, are somewhat similar,

34
00:01:21,206 --> 00:01:22,774
but the wau themselves are different.

35
00:01:23,832 --> 00:01:26,523
The Perlis wau is different, the Johor wau is different,

36
00:01:26,603 --> 00:01:27,921
and the Kelantan wau is also different.

37
00:01:28,439 --> 00:01:32,312
Kelantan wau... every state has

38
00:01:32,392 --> 00:01:33,292
its own state wau.

39
00:01:33,372 --> 00:01:35,322
Every state in Malaysia has a wau.

40
00:01:35,402 --> 00:01:36,652
But they are all different.

41
00:01:36,732 --> 00:01:40,924
For example, Johor has the peacock wau (Wau Merak).

42
00:01:41,535 --> 00:01:44,392
Here in Selangor, it's the ship wau (Wau Kapal).

43
00:01:44,975 --> 00:01:46,091
Every state.

44
00:01:46,171 --> 00:01:48,121
Perlis is the eagle wau (Wau Helang), which Pak Non makes.

45
00:01:48,415 --> 00:01:51,152
Kelantan is the quail wau (Wau Burung Puyuh).

46
00:01:51,315 --> 00:01:53,544
So the wau from different states are not the same.

47
00:01:55,151 --> 00:01:56,668
The wau that Pak Non makes,

48
00:01:57,211 --> 00:02:00,406
you could say for Malaysian wau, Pak Non makes all of them.

49
00:02:00,523 --> 00:02:02,373
There are 3 types of Malaysian wau.

50
00:02:02,453 --> 00:02:03,988
If it's a Malaysian wau,

51
00:02:04,068 --> 00:02:06,568
no individual state can claim it as entirely theirs.

52
00:02:06,648 --> 00:02:08,022
One of them is the moon kite (Wau Bulan),

53
00:02:08,117 --> 00:02:10,217
the Wau Bulan that is on our coins.

54
00:02:10,417 --> 00:02:12,710
That is a Malaysian wau. Another is the cat wau (Wau Kucing),

55
00:02:12,790 --> 00:02:14,690
also a Malaysian wau, and the other is the Wau Jala Budi.

56
00:02:14,777 --> 00:02:15,577
Malaysian wau.

57
00:02:16,496 --> 00:02:17,780
But for Pak Non,

58
00:02:17,860 --> 00:02:20,283
Pak Non makes all three of these Malaysian wau types.

59
00:02:20,996 --> 00:02:23,446
The Wau Jala Budi that Pak Non makes flies beautifully.

60
00:02:24,388 --> 00:02:25,733
At least to Pak Non.

61
00:02:25,868 --> 00:02:27,568
Other people might think differently, perhaps.

62
00:02:27,728 --> 00:02:28,878
For Pak Non, it's the Wau Jala Budi.

63
00:02:29,926 --> 00:02:30,885
This Wau Jala Budi,

64
00:02:30,965 --> 00:02:33,165
when Pak Non used to make it for competitions,

65
00:02:33,468 --> 00:02:35,600
the wau would usually stay right above Pak Non's head.

66
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:37,335
It ascends right towards us.

67
00:02:37,888 --> 00:02:38,973
It doesn't drift far away.

68
00:02:40,571 --> 00:02:43,294
So that is the one Pak Non makes a bit more of

69
00:02:43,374 --> 00:02:44,308
among those 3 wau.

70
00:02:45,131 --> 00:02:48,080
As for motifs, Pak Non knows many; Pak Non has made a lot of wau,

71
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:49,738
Pak Non even makes the water spinach (kangkung) motif.

72
00:02:49,818 --> 00:02:51,418
Pak Non makes the kangkung motif.

73
00:02:51,498 --> 00:02:53,548
But this isn't the vegetable kangkung,

74
00:02:53,771 --> 00:02:56,908
it's the kangkung on the beach, the one on the sand.

75
00:02:57,480 --> 00:03:00,202
The kangkung found in rivers or swamps,

76
00:03:03,556 --> 00:03:04,541
The kangkung by

77
00:03:05,096 --> 00:03:08,110
the beach, that one truly makes a beautiful motif.

78
00:03:08,190 --> 00:03:10,609
Besides that, Pak Non also does the morning glory (seri pagi) motif,

79
00:03:10,689 --> 00:03:12,918
the one that intertwines on fences, you know.

80
00:03:13,481 --> 00:03:16,739
Its flowers are purple; Pak Non makes that.

81
00:03:17,297 --> 00:03:19,147
Then, Pak Non also makes the bean tendril (sulur kacang) motif.

82
00:03:19,563 --> 00:03:21,462
You could say Pak Non has many motifs.

83
00:03:21,737 --> 00:03:24,162
Pak Non has been making wau for 60 years, so

84
00:03:24,537 --> 00:03:26,787
I can't even remember them all; there are dozens of motifs.

85
00:03:27,357 --> 00:03:30,716
But Pak Non's absolute favorite

86
00:03:31,257 --> 00:03:32,742
is the kangkung.

87
00:03:33,409 --> 00:03:35,718
The kangkung found right near the seaside.

88
00:03:35,798 --> 00:03:36,850
That beach kangkung.

89
00:03:37,809 --> 00:03:39,130
It's beautiful to look at.

90
00:03:39,629 --> 00:03:42,468
Its flowers, when they bloom, are beautiful to look at.

91
00:03:42,749 --> 00:03:44,370
Its vines creeping around,

92
00:03:44,949 --> 00:03:46,899
curving here and there, that kangkung.

93
00:03:47,391 --> 00:03:49,741
In Kuala Perlis, you can find it on the beaches.

94
00:03:50,391 --> 00:03:52,408
This big wau,

95
00:03:52,851 --> 00:03:54,064
for the Perlis Museum.

96
00:03:54,751 --> 00:03:56,486
They came to order it from Pak Non.

97
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,874
That huge wau.

98
00:03:59,165 --> 00:04:02,090
They contacted Kraftangan (Handicraft), they called them

99
00:04:02,170 --> 00:04:03,420
and all. "Can it be done?..

100
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:04,885
..or not?" Of course we could do it,

101
00:04:04,965 --> 00:04:06,065
but it had to be 30 feet long.

102
00:04:06,865 --> 00:04:08,411
But we had to calculate the cost first,

103
00:04:08,491 --> 00:04:10,365
then we'd make it; it could definitely be done.

104
00:04:10,914 --> 00:04:12,974
Pak Non made that 30-foot wau, one piece.

105
00:04:13,345 --> 00:04:15,234
But it took a month's time.

106
00:04:16,448 --> 00:04:17,698
But we didn't use paper.

107
00:04:17,778 --> 00:04:20,319
Paper wouldn't stick well; just sticking it a bit,

108
00:04:20,399 --> 00:04:21,399
it could tear,

109
00:04:21,479 --> 00:04:23,988
for a 30-foot size we used thin white cloth.

110
00:04:25,468 --> 00:04:27,568
But it turned out beautiful; it had to be beautiful like that.

111
00:04:28,688 --> 00:04:30,228
The pattern was just like a regular wau.

112
00:04:31,698 --> 00:04:34,696
But we couldn't bring it inside the museum.

113
00:04:35,618 --> 00:04:37,400
They just displayed it outside.

114
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:39,830
If we wanted to bring it into the museum, we had to dismantle it.

115
00:04:39,910 --> 00:04:41,210
Dismantle and reassemble it.

116
00:04:41,956 --> 00:04:43,692
Then it got into the museum.

117
00:04:43,776 --> 00:04:45,543
After that, as for

118
00:04:45,996 --> 00:04:49,341
another one in Johor, at Pasir Gudang,

119
00:04:49,836 --> 00:04:50,840
the peacock wau,

120
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:51,670
the Johor peacock wau

121
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:52,720
belonging to His Majesty,

122
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:55,480
Pak Non made it for the International

123
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:56,910
Kite Festival.

124
00:04:57,091 --> 00:04:59,091
For that one, Pak Non flew it with His Majesty.

125
00:04:59,171 --> 00:05:00,759
When His Majesty launched it,

126
00:05:01,020 --> 00:05:03,294
Pak Non held the string with His Majesty.

127
00:05:03,820 --> 00:05:06,329
Another one, at the Langkawi Craft Complex,

128
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:08,860
during the time of this doctor...

129
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:11,160
Datuk Mazeb wanted to officiate the opening

130
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:12,646
of the Langkawi Craft Complex.

131
00:05:12,941 --> 00:05:16,372
Pak Non made one for that, 15 feet in size.

132
00:05:17,048 --> 00:05:20,202
During the opening ceremony of the Langkawi Craft Complex,

133
00:05:20,282 --> 00:05:23,126
that wau was the one they pulled up.

134
00:05:23,908 --> 00:05:25,306
That's the one that got damaged.

135
00:05:26,963 --> 00:05:29,396
From Kraftangan (Handicraft Malaysia), Pak Non has received

136
00:05:29,963 --> 00:05:33,307
titles twice already.

137
00:05:33,387 --> 00:05:35,776
The first one they gave was Tukang Ulung (Master Craftsman).

138
00:05:36,543 --> 00:05:37,893
Kraftangan gave it to Pak Non.

139
00:05:38,443 --> 00:05:41,556
The second one, just recently,

140
00:05:42,103 --> 00:05:45,659
was Adiguru. So Pak Non received two from Kraftangan.

141
00:05:46,681 --> 00:05:47,981
Pak Non's wau, Pak Non

142
00:05:48,061 --> 00:05:50,280
has brought them to many countries.

143
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:52,960
But it was Kraftangan that brought Pak Non.

144
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:55,859
To London, Pak Non has gone.

145
00:05:56,732 --> 00:05:57,732
To do demonstrations there.

146
00:05:57,812 --> 00:05:59,367
Not to compete in matches,

147
00:05:59,447 --> 00:06:00,547
just to do demonstrations there.

148
00:06:01,192 --> 00:06:03,345
Pak Non also went to France.

149
00:06:04,132 --> 00:06:05,683
Pak Non also went to Korea.

150
00:06:06,632 --> 00:06:10,385
So, many places. Pak Non has gone to China 3 times already.

151
00:06:11,402 --> 00:06:14,288
But Pak Non went to do demonstrations, not to compete.

152
00:06:15,602 --> 00:06:16,768
Australia, once.

153
00:06:18,342 --> 00:06:19,233
Over in Australia.

154
00:06:20,092 --> 00:06:21,192
You could say it's a lot,

155
00:06:21,272 --> 00:06:22,763
many countries. As for Thailand, you could

156
00:06:22,843 --> 00:06:24,343
say Pak Non goes there often.

157
00:06:24,815 --> 00:06:27,484
Pak Non has been the Champion in Thailand 3 times.

158
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:30,722
Got a trophy there, a challenge trophy.

159
00:06:30,802 --> 00:06:32,610
Pak Non's hope is, this craft,

160
00:06:33,190 --> 00:06:35,395
this making of wau,

161
00:06:35,475 --> 00:06:37,525
up until now, here in Perlis,

162
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:39,855
Pak Non has taught many who can now make them.

163
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:41,400
They can make them, they can carve the patterns,

164
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:42,915
if they were to compete with Pak Non,

165
00:06:42,995 --> 00:06:45,390
these students of Pak Non, Pak Non might even lose.

166
00:06:45,470 --> 00:06:46,520
They are young people,

167
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:48,120
there are many of them in Perlis.

168
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:51,410
But in Johor, there are also many of Pak Non's students,

169
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:52,870
around Pasir Gudang.

170
00:06:53,835 --> 00:06:56,496
So if we look at it so far,

171
00:06:56,576 --> 00:06:59,603
if we look at the states where I've taught,

172
00:06:59,683 --> 00:07:01,962
there are indeed many people flying wau now.

173
00:07:02,940 --> 00:07:04,040
In Perlis, you could say

174
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:05,500
during the dry season,

175
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:07,580
there are almost always competitions held.

176
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:10,440
Wau flying competitions.

177
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:13,930
Some have patterns and some don't.

178
00:07:15,818 --> 00:07:19,021
But Pak Non feels that, as of right now,

179
00:07:19,398 --> 00:07:21,781
it's hard for it to go extinct. It won't go extinct.

180
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:25,478
If anything, it won't go extinct for another 45 years.

181
00:07:25,558 --> 00:07:26,658
Those students of Pak Non,

182
00:07:26,738 --> 00:07:28,538
many in Perlis can make them.

183
00:07:30,318 --> 00:07:31,801
That is Pak Non's hope.